{"number":1298,"title":"A parked decision states its options as checkboxes, and the next scheduler run reads the answer","body":"A run that parks at `task:status:needs-human-decision` today leaves a person two things to do that the machine could carry: reconstruct what the choice actually was, and translate their answer into a label edit (strip the park, apply `task:status:waiting-for-executor`). The answer itself is then lost — the resumed run reads nothing about what was decided.

Wanted (owner):

- a park whose remedy is a **choice** writes the choice as checkboxes on the item, one box per option;
- a ticked box is read by the **next scheduler run**, which resumes the item — the answer carried into the resumed run rather than discarded;
- **closing the issue** is the other exit, and works without any of this;
- **follow-up work is blocked on the parked item**, so both exits release it.

Scope of this issue: model the flow in the dispatch simulator, confirm it fits the scheduler run&#39;s existing job structure, and change `docs/tasks-dispatch/DESIGN.md` (plus SCENARIOS and the sim&#39;s coverage map). Engine implementation is separate work.","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/1298","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","assignees":[],"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-08-23T18:22:40Z","updated_at":"2026-08-23T18:22:40Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":true,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":1,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":1,"references":[{"number":1299,"title":"Model the decision ballot: a parked choice, answered in place","state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/1299","repository":"missingbulb/Claudinite"}]}}

